              "Emergency water systems were built by international aid organisations. Food is delivered by trucks and helicopters to remote villages. But the deeper problem \u2014 climate change \u2014 can\u2019t be fixed by one delivery of water. It requires the whole world to act.",
              "REPORT 4 \u2014 TURKEY AND SYRIA, FEBRUARY 2023",
              "Two massive earthquakes struck southern Turkey and northern Syria within 9 hours of each other. Over 55,000 people were killed. More than 100,000 buildings collapsed or were seriously damaged. It was one of the worst earthquakes of the 21st century so far.",
              "But the response was extraordinary. Rescue teams from over 90 countries were flown in. Thousands of tonnes of aid were shipped by ordinary citizens across the globe. A little boy was pulled from the rubble after 40 hours, still smiling. His photo went around the world in minutes.",
